WEBVTT

00:00:09.375 --> 00:00:10.799
Hi there.

00:00:10.799 --> 00:00:13.791
Welcome to this video
where we are going to explore

00:00:13.919 --> 00:00:17.039
what authentication means
in the digital world.

00:00:17.999 --> 00:00:25.839
The goal of the video is help you to understand 
why authentication is needed every day.

00:00:29.743 --> 00:00:33.631
Computers and apps cannot 
recognize people like humans can.

00:00:33.791 --> 00:00:37.823
They cannot see faces, hear voices,
or recognize emotions.

00:00:38.351 --> 00:00:43.023
Because of this, systems need a clear way
to know who is using them.

00:00:43.711 --> 00:00:49.263
Without this, anyone 
could pretend to be anyone else.

00:00:52.831 --> 00:00:57.311
Proof is needed so systems can check
that the right person is logging in.

00:00:58.271 --> 00:01:02.063
This proof helps protect accounts
from strangers and attackers.

00:01:02.623 --> 00:01:06.191
Without proof, personal information
would not be safe.

00:01:06.943 --> 00:01:09.951
Authentication provides that proof.

00:01:13.999 --> 00:01:18.607
Authentication is the process of proving
who you are to a digital system.

00:01:19.039 --> 00:01:23.167
It shows that your digital identity
is real and belongs to you.

00:01:23.967 --> 00:01:26.959
Authentication happens
every time you log in.

00:01:27.087 --> 00:01:30.079
It is a key part of online safety.

00:01:30.479 --> 00:01:33.487
Think about entering a school or library.

00:01:33.727 --> 00:01:37.567
You may need to show an ID or
tell your name to prove you belong there.

00:01:38.287 --> 00:01:40.959
Authentication works the same way online.

00:01:40.959 --> 00:01:43.727
It checks that you are allowed to enter.

00:01:43.727 --> 00:01:47.807
Authentication exists
to stop strangers from accessing accounts.

00:01:47.839 --> 00:01:52.287
It protects messages,
photos, schoolwork, and game progress.

00:01:52.959 --> 00:01:56.847
Without authentication,
digital spaces would not be private.

00:01:57.039 --> 00:01:59.679
Everyone's data would be at risk.

00:01:59.679 --> 00:02:03.471
Authentication protects
many types of digital information.

00:02:03.951 --> 00:02:07.743
This includes emails, messages,
files, and personal data.

00:02:08.303 --> 00:02:11.711
It also protects
your digital reputation and identity.

00:02:17.055 --> 00:02:20.575
Strong authentication keeps these things secure.

00:02:20.735 --> 00:02:23.743
Passwords are the most common
authentication method.

00:02:24.255 --> 00:02:27.935
A password is a secret
that only the real user should know.

00:02:28.783 --> 00:02:32.463
Systems check the password to confirm identity.

00:02:32.575 --> 00:02:35.503
Keeping passwords
secret is very important.

00:02:35.503 --> 00:02:38.303
Some systems use more than just passwords.

00:02:38.303 --> 00:02:42.542
They may use codes sent to devices,
security cards, or fingerprints.

00:02:42.654 --> 00:02:45.022
These methods add extra protection.

00:02:45.022 --> 00:02:48.014
They make it harder 
for attackers to get in.

00:02:52.574 --> 00:02:55.566
Attackers often
try to break authentication.

00:02:55.566 --> 00:02:58.606
They may guess passwords 
or trick people into sharing them.

00:02:59.214 --> 00:03:02.206
Their goal is to pretend 
to be someone else.

00:03:02.542 --> 00:03:05.534
Good authentication makes this difficult.

00:03:06.430 --> 00:03:10.158
Sharing passwords breaks 
authentication completely.

00:03:10.638 --> 00:03:13.630
It gives someone else 
access to your identity.

00:03:14.078 --> 00:03:17.198
Even trusted friends
should not know your password.

00:03:17.838 --> 00:03:19.790
Passwords must stay private.

00:03:19.790 --> 00:03:22.478
Strong authentication
makes accounts safer.

00:03:22.478 --> 00:03:25.470
It slows attackers down and can stop them.

00:03:25.710 --> 00:03:28.718
Using good methods protects
digital identity.

00:03:28.958 --> 00:03:31.438
Strong authentication is a smart habit.

00:03:31.438 --> 00:03:33.998
You play an important role
in authentication.

00:03:33.998 --> 00:03:36.990
Your choices help keep systems secure.

00:03:37.118 --> 00:03:40.158
Choosing good secrets 
and protecting them matters.

00:03:40.238 --> 00:03:42.990
Safe behavior supports authentication.

00:03:48.142 --> 00:03:52.094
Authentication is how systems 
check who you are.

00:03:52.158 --> 00:03:54.910
It protects accounts and personal data.

00:03:54.910 --> 00:03:58.702
Without it, digital spaces 
would not be safe.

00:03:58.814 --> 00:04:03.918
Authentication helps 
keep your digital life secure.

00:04:06.190 --> 00:04:07.758
Thank you for watching.

00:04:07.758 --> 00:04:10.718
Do not forget to watch
other videos in our series.